Verified":false},{"id":"fara-2023-2-p270-r7331-0-0-0","country":"SL","origin":"SIERRA LEONE","category":"lobby","measure":"fara-receipts","amount":null,"year":null,"periodEnd":null,"periodMonths":null,"reportYear":2023,"reportHalf":2,"recipient":"Ifrah Law, PLLC","principal":"Government of Sierra Leone","governmentSource":null,"services":"Legal and Other Services/Lobbying","description":"Activities: The registrant represents FARA registrant Jerry Torres (Reg No 7312) relating to his advisory relationship with the President of Sierra Leone, Julius Maada Wonie Bio. Through Mr. Torres, the registrant has identified three areas of assistance which would form the basis of its relationship with Sierra Leone. These areas include: investigating and evaluating the status of President Bio's immigration status with U.S. authorities; evaluating and providing training to prosecutors and police in Sierra Leone; and, investigating whether prosecutor and police training could be provided to Sierra Leone through the United States Departments of State and/or Justice. This would likely involve communicating with State or Justice Department officials about the possibility of expanding current training efforts in Sierra Leone and would start with the appropriate official at the Overseas Prosecutorial Development and Training Office of the Department of Justice. Finances: None Reported","source":"fara-2023-2","locator":"PDF p. 270; amount p. 270","page":270,"amountPage":270,"registration":"7331","duplicateOf":null,"review":"structured-extraction","periodText":"None Reported","cashVerified":false},{"id":"fara-2023-2-p270-r7312-1-0-0","country":"SL","origin":"SIERRA LEONE","category":"lobby","measure":"fara-receipts","amount":null,"year":null,"periodEnd":null,"periodMonths":null,"reportYear":2023,"reportHalf":2,"recipient":"Jerry W. Torres","principal":"Julius Maada Wonie Bio","governmentSource":null,"services":"Lobbying","description":"Activities: The registrant will serve as the National Security Advisor to the foreign principal who is the President of Sierra Leone. The registrant will advise and assist the foreign principal and any designated representatives of Sierra Leone in promoting that country's efforts to better secure information, develop cyber investigative and offensive capabilities, participate in global and regional security efforts, develop its economy, and strengthen its political relations with the United States. In addition, the registrant will present information to the United States media and Congressional representatives to strengthen United States-Sierra Leone relations and possibly develop social media or website platforms to advance the interests of the nation of Sierra Leone. The registrant may serve as a liaison on behalf of the foreign principal and possibly facilitate introductions to representatives of Congress and other branches of the United States Government. Finances: None Reported","source":"fara-2023-2","locator":"PDF p. 270; amount p. 270","page":270,"amountPage":270,"registration":"7312","duplicateOf":null,"review":"structured-extraction","periodText":"None Reported","cashVerified":false},{"id":"fara-2023-2-p271-r6170-2-0-0","country":"SL","origin":"SIERRA LEONE","category":"media","measure":"fara-receipts","amount":71600.0,"year":2023,"periodEnd":"2023-12-31","periodMonths":6,"reportYear":2023,"reportHalf":2,"recipient":"Mercury Public Affairs, LLC","principal":"Republic of Sierra Leone","governmentSource":null,"services":"Media Relations","description":"Activities: The registrant performed government relations, public relations, and communications advice and services, including outreach to government officials and US media. Finances: $71,600.00 for the six month period ending December 31, 2023","source":"fara-2023-2","locator":"PDF p. 271; amount p. 271","page":271,"amountPage":271,"registration":"6170","duplicateOf":null,"review":"structured-extraction","periodText":"$71,600.00 for the six month period ending 